WEBVTT

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.580
I'm home.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.860
Welcome back.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.300
What's this?

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.680
It's from Grandpa.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.030
He says he's not using it anymore.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.760
"Camping gear."

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:51.520
Black Holes and 
the Grand Cosmos

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.100
Rin.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:07.750
Do you have your books?

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.820
Yeah, I do.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.300
Stay safe, okay?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.110
Okay.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.240
Off you go.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.140
See you later.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:09.180
<b>(2) Episode 1 
Curry Noodles Are the Best Travel Companion</b>

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.930
Hello. We have a reservation under "Shima."

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.220
Day camping, correct?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.280
Is this your first time camping?

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.180
Yes.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.050
If you have any questions, feel free to ask.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.190
Okay.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.540
What a nice place.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.810
Need help setting up the tent?

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.350
I'll try doing it myself.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:53.780
All right.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.100
Well, I'll be up at the lodge.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.760
I'll come get you this evening.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.730
Thanks.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.620
Okay.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:28.670
It's hard...

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:34.940
Shoot!

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.100
Gently...

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.330
Done.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:58.920
In Pursuit of OOPArts

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.740
<i>It's kind of cold...</i>

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.170
<i>I should try making a campfire.</i>

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.310
<i>There's a ton of it around.</i>

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.280
<i>So much to burn...</i>

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.750
Huh?

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.920
<i>It's not lighting.</i>

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.650
<i>Maybe I need more flame.</i>

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.510
<i>It's getting even colder.</i>

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.290
E-Excuse me...

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:53.680
Ah, it's harder to start a 
fire with thicker branches.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:05.110
That'll get you started, but it'll burn 
more consistently if you make a fire pit.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.110
You'll also need these.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.000
Pine cones?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.490
Hello

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.490
Hello!

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:16.300
Use them as fire starters,
and place the thinner branches on first.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.280
Thank you for your help.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.800
It's so warm.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.760
<i>I guess I should have brought 
some tools to cut wood.</i>

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:37.640
<i>But now that I have a fire thanks to that guy...</i>

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.900
<i>I'm going to make the 
classic camp meal: curry rice.</i>

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.820
<i>The finished roux goes here.</i>

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.030
<i>Next, we boil some rice.</i>

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.810
<i>Did I do it right?</i>

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.580
<i>It's hard!</i>

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.370
<i>Sorry, kids.</i>

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.580
<i>I'll deal with you later.</i>

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.830
<i>It won't come off!</i>

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.290
<i>It's evening already.</i>

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.800
<i>Nothing went right...</i>

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.650
<i>I didn't have any time to read.</i>

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.860
My butt hurts.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.860
Gurrrgle

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.910
<i>I guess I'll just have to call it curry soup.</i>

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.120
Home

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.570
Hello? Mom?

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:29.950
<i>Rin, how's it going? Are you staying warm?</i>

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.050
I'm fine.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.720
I got a fire started, too.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.290
<i>Have you eaten?</i>

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:40.240
Yeah, I made some food... sort of.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.140
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.980
<i>I put emergency food in your backpack.</i>

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.720
<i>Have that if you're still hungry.</i>

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.680
Thanks, Mom.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:00.810
Five, four, three, two, one...

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:01.780
Done.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.660
Time to eat.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:45.130
Was this stuff always so good?

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.080
Hey, wait up!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:06.430
<i>I thought I'd done enough research, 
but actually doing it is totally different.</i>

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.650
<i>I didn't get to read, either.</i>

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:41.350
<i>Woodcutting tools, and I guess a chair...</i>

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.040
<i>I wonder if my allowance will cover those.</i>

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.520
Nadeshiko!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.230
Come on!

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.580
Wait up!

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:35.370
Next is...

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.590
Takano-san!

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:39.680
You're working hard.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.190
Another cold day, huh?

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:42.780
Hello!

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.420
It sure is cold, isn't it?

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:49.200
Seeing young folks deliver letters 
really sets the mood for December.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.700
Kyoto Hirokawa Tea

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:51.700
Here you go. Hang in there.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.210
Thank you!

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.960
I'm all done!

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.840
That was fast, Kagamihara-san. 
You've gotten used to it already?

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:02.960
Perfectly!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.490
I'll see you again this afternoon, then.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:06.220
Yup!

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.120
Hey!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.220
Oh, Ena-chan!

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.140
Good work.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.580
You, too.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.200
Wanna go have lunch?

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.480
Yeah!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.180
Stew, huh?

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.540
Yeah. Overnight stew.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:27.200
You made lots of food, huh?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.990
They say an army marches on its stomach.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.240
Time to eat!

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.250
Ena-chan, how's work inside?

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.580
I spend all day staring at addresses.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:49.060
But at least I get to be warm the whole time.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.260
Oh, yeah?

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:51.880
How about you?

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:53.890
I'm getting the hang of it.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.380
Someone even gave me tea today.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.150
That's cool.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.400
And there's this one house 
that has a tiny mini-shiba.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.720
It's so cute.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.140
I can't wait to deliver there.

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:09.400
Yeah?

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:12.220
I guess you won't be lonely, then. That's good.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:13.300
Yeah.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.160
It's just a temp job. 
We gotta work for our money!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:19.620
Do you already know what
 you're going to spend it on?

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.420
Yeah. Hang on...

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:22.600
Here.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.730
This gas lantern I found at the shop.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.420
It's so cute and retro.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.280
Hey, this is nice.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:33.080
I've actually been looking 
at camping gear lately, too.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.060
Yeah?

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.920
There's so much different 
camping gear out there.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:40.190
I can't stop searching for stuff.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.670
Then I started wanting a tent.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:47.210
I might buy something, too, once I get paid.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:50.600
The Outclub's ready for you anytime.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.700
Nah, I can't quit the going home club just yet.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.770
Aw...

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:02.500
Hey, Nadeshiko.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.710
How's work?

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.430
Hey!

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:06.860
I'm getting used to it.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.120
How about you? Are you busy?

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.970
Busy as hell!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:15.720
<b>Kawamoto  Liquors</b>

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.900
Liquor sells like crazy around year end.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:15.720
I'll be working full-time until the fourth.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:19.980
Winter break will be over by the 
time I'm done with my homework.

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.120
We won't be getting any breaks 
since we're in the busy season.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.260
Let's bust our butts!

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.700
Huh? I got the second and third off.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.640
Say what?

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.620
Yeah, I have the third and fourth off.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.000
I'm off from the first to the third.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:42.360
I've got the 31st to the fourth.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.250
What're you all doing on your days off?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:50.280
I'm going to sleep in until noon, then make 
my New Year's shrine visit with Chikuwa.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.260
After that, I think I'll go 
to the shopping center.

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:56.920
I'm hanging out with my family 
at my relatives' place in Takayama.

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:59.020
Hida Takayama is so nice.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:01.040
Are you going anywhere, Nadeshiko?

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:04.150
Yeah, I'm going to go my 
grandma's place at Lake Hamana.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:07.430
Does that mean you'll be eating eel?

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:08.640
Hee hee!

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:12.280
There is indeed a delicious eel 
place nearby, ma'am!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.770
I'm going solo camping again.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:18.000
I haven't decided where yet, 
but somewhere by the beach. Maybe Izu.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.790
Izu camping? Nice!

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.750
I'm thinking of watching 
the sun rise over the sea.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.920
Sunrise over the sea is so pretty.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:31.520
Speaking of Izu, I saw on TV that the golden-eye 
snapper burgers in Shimoda are really good.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:33.690
Huh, I should check that out.

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:34.800
Oh, also...

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:39.130
<i>Abject time poverty!</i>

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:40.130
<i>Why?!</i>

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:43.440
<i>Has my winter break met its demise?!</i>

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.840
Chiaki, should I buy you some local food?

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:51.150
I'll get you something, too, Aki.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:54.500
I'll buy you some eel snacks, Aki-chan!

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.820
Y-You guys!

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.270
All right!

00:16:58.270 --> 00:17:00.450
I'll hold down the fort in Minobu!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:04.960
I shall patiently await your
 (and your gifts') homecoming!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.380
We're busy today. Focus on the work, okay?

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.750
I'm sorry.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:17.340
<b>Takeda Bookstore</b>

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:17.340
Welcome.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.840
<i>Izu, Izu, Izu...</i>

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:24.850
<i>Zui, Zui...</i>

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:28.860
Izu

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.860
<i>Should I go to Nishiizu via Numazu?</i>

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.610
<i>Or should I go through 
Izunokuni and check out Ito?</i>

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:38.360
<i>Actually, taking the Amagi Pass to
 Minamiizu wouldn't be bad, either.</i>

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.740
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.750
<b>Menu of the Month</b>

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:50.310
<i>Soba, huh?</i>

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:53.400
<i>I'm leaving on the 31st.</i>

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:56.260
<i>Maybe I should have New Year's 
soba for my camp meal.</i>

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:00.990
<i>I gained some weight on our 
Christmas camp, after all.</i>

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.330
<i>Soba would be lighter.</i>

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:06.770
So you're headed to Izu this time, huh?

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:12.150
How about going through Numazu 
along the water and past Heda?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.690
Cape Mihama looks beautiful 
from the high ground,

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:19.940
and the Nishiizu skyline is 
gorgeous. It's a nice route.

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:25.290
Though the roads in Izu might 
be busy during New Year's.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.280
A lot of people visit from Tokyo.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.540
That would suck.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.520
If you want to see the ocean,
 how about Omaezaki?

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:36.890
The Pacific looks beautiful 
from the lighthouse hill.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:38.800
Omaezaki, huh?

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.550
Just don't get into an accident, Rin.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.310
That's the one thing I'm worried about.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.550
I know.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:48.060
I'll avoid the busy roads as much as I can.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:50.890
Oh, and Grandpa's coming on the third.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:52.770
Be home by then.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.440
Okay. Don't worry.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.280
He said he's looking forward to seeing you.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:06.640
<i>Okay, so where can I camp around Omaezaki?</i>

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.580
<i>This one's closed for the season.</i>

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:14.800
<i>This one's a bit far, but there's 
a campground by the water in Iwata.</i>

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.600
<i>Are they open in the winter?</i>

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:19.220
<i>They are! They're open year-round.</i>

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:21.640
<i>Iwata?</i>

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:27.220
<i>There's a nasty monster in Iwata 
that torments the villagers.</i>

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:30.990
<i>Me and Hayatarou here are 
going to teach him a lesson.</i>

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:35.150
Iwata, Hayatarou...

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:42.040
<i>Enshrined at Mitsuke-Tenjin Shrine in 
Iwata is the spirit dog Shippeitarou.</i>

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:47.990
<i>Shippeitarou is lovingly known to the locals 
of Komagane by the name "Hayatarou."</i>

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.250
<i></i>The<i> Hayatarou, huh?</i>

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:58.760
<i>And Shippeitarou the Third is a real pet 
that lives at Mitsuke-Tenjin Shrine.</i>

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:01.320
<i>A spirit dog that I can actually meet...</i>

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.510
<i>All right.</i>

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.770
I'm going on another
\hdog shrine visit

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.220
Rin-chan!

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:28.180
Rin-chan!

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.010
Morning!

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.070
Are you heading out?

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:49.630
Yeah.

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:53.120
That's right. You live
 around here, don't you?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:54.950
Going to work already?

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:58.570
Not yet, but I woke up a little too early,

00:21:58.570 --> 00:22:01.640
so I bought some snacks for break time.

00:22:05.480 --> 00:22:06.640
Here you go.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.910
Curry noodles for your travels.

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:20.790
Thanks.

00:22:31.420 --> 00:22:33.480
Well, good luck at work.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:36.160
Be safe, Rin-chan.

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:38.870
Bye, then.

00:22:39.410 --> 00:22:40.690
See you later.

00:22:53.030 --> 00:22:55.520
<b>Inuinu Inuko-san</b>

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:55.520
Inuinu Inuko-san!

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:01.760
Hey, you started calling Aoi-chan "Inuko" 
because you misread her name, right?

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:03.580
Yeah, something like that.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:05.530
It wasn't just that.

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:09.950
I lived in Inuyama City, where my family 
ran a dog café called Café Inuyama,

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:13.130
plus my whole family was 
born in the year of the dog.

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:16.100
What?! A dog café in Inuyama City
 called Café Inuyama?

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:18.160
And your whole family's born
 in the year of the dog?!

00:23:18.510 --> 00:23:21.590
And this is my puppy.

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:25.040
Seriously, that's enough.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:35.300
Next Episode

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:35.300
<b>New Year's Solo Camper Girl</b>

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:42.020
When camping...

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:42.020
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:42.020
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:42.020
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!
